THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE AND ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

Dextop — github.com/NarYuki/Dextop
  License: GPL-3.0-or-later.
  Computer mode's privileged runtime is adapted from Dextop: the handshake that
  hands the shell helper's Binder to the app through a ContentProvider, the
  SHELL_UID gate on that provider, the transaction-forwarding model that lets the
  app reach a framework service with shell identity, the `app_process` launch
  command, and the reflective trusted-virtual-display creation with its degrading
  flag ladder. Adapted files name Dextop in their header. This is why the project
  is GPL-3.0-or-later.

Kadb — github.com/flyfishxu/Kadb (com.flyfishxu:kadb)
  License: Apache-2.0.
  Used to pair with, and connect to, the phone's own Wireless debugging endpoint.

spake2-java — github.com/Flyfish233/spake2-java (com.github.Flyfish233:spake2-java)
  License: Apache-2.0.
  SPAKE2 key exchange for ADB pairing; a transitive dependency of Kadb.

HiddenApiBypass — github.com/LSPosed/AndroidHiddenApiBypass
  License: Apache-2.0.
  Lets the shell-level helper reach the hidden display and input APIs.

scrcpy — github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy
  License: Apache-2.0.
  No scrcpy code is included. Its approach informed computer mode's design:
  creating a virtual display as the shell user and launching an app onto it,
  and injecting input to a specific display. Credit to Romain Vimont (@rom1v).

Android-Dex — github.com/Shrey113/Android-Dex
  Proprietary; no code is used. Acknowledged for the per-app-display and
  notification/heads-up ideas discussed during design.
